<!DOCTYPE Menu PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD Menu 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/menu-spec/1.0/menu.dtd">
<!--
██╗  ██╗██████╗  ██████╗ ███████╗
██║ ██╔╝██╔══██╗██╔═══██╗██╔════╝
█████╔╝ ██║  ██║██║   ██║███████╗
██╔═██╗ ██║  ██║██║   ██║╚════██║
██║  ██╗██████╔╝╚██████╔╝███████║
╚═╝  ╚═╝╚═════╝  ╚═════╝ ╚══════╝
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
  The menu's Boxes category.

`kdos-box export` writes a launcher for an application inside a box with
Categories=X-KDOS-Box and nothing else, because the box's own entry is the
distribution's and its categories are guesses about another system. No main
category means Plasma's menu files the launcher under Lost & Found; this
merge file gathers them under Boxes instead, beside the main categories.
A launcher a pack's genlaunchers writes keeps the application's own
categories and is filed with them.

Merged into plasma-applications.menu through its <DefaultMergeDirs/>, as
kio-library's Library category is.
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
-->
<Menu>
  <Name>Applications</Name>
  <Menu>
    <Name>Boxes</Name>
    <Directory>kdos-boxes.directory</Directory>
    <Include>
      <Category>X-KDOS-Box</Category>
    </Include>
  </Menu>
</Menu>
